aight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T15:25:12-07:00","id":1537227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537226#post1537226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well only if you want to discuss V5. LIke I said, V20 is the last defending outpost of lore and history for the WOD.<br /> <br /> I'm also getting caught up on their work for W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>i respect your decision","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T15:38:53-07:00","id":1537229,"title":"","content":"If the writers focused on the refinement of the product rather than the progression of the product, V5 would have been fine in my opinion. But that sadly isn't what happened.<br /> <br /> Anyways, welcome back to fold of V20, the meetings start at 9 pm with complementary blood dolls and the nostalgia discussion is slated for the rest of the evening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T15:42:31-07:00","id":1537230,"title":"","content":"The only NPCs I really like are Hesha and Aisling Sturbridge and I have a feeling that they won't have much of a presence in the current setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:04:21-07:00","id":1537233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537230#post1537230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only NPCs I really like are Hesha and Aisling Sturbridge and I have a feeling that they won't have much of a presence in the current setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aisling shows up in every single one of the Coteries games so she's actually gotten better than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:37:38-07:00","id":1537236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537224#post1537224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, for me, the problem is I was never in it for the rules so much as the characters and seeing how they evolve.<br /> <br /> I actually really enjoyed the New York visual novels and LA by Night primarily because they showed how the settings changed from the books.<br /> <br /> Knowing that's never going to happen again is sad. Lucita and Jan Pieterszoon may be dead or they may be not but they'll never have a big role in the books again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You look like you need a hug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:39:02-07:00","id":1537237,"title":"","content":"I am sorry, actually, as I know how much you were invested on it.<br /> <br /> V20 is the way to go for any sort of continuation of the old setting, and Requiem 2nd is a far better new setting. Trying to be both and none at the same time was a bad idea for V5.<br /> <br /> All we can do now is to hope that they someday notice the lines they can still invest in and let OPP do its job with them in peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T19:09:13-07:00","id":1537242,"title":"","content":"That's too bad. It was the Sabbat book that killed V5 for me, so I've moved back to V20. That said there's still some metaplot in V5 that I like (the Ministry) or that I'm okay with (the Hecata) or think there's some potential with modification (the Second Inquisition) and bring some of that stuff over to my V20 games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T08:44:10-07:00","id":1537260,"title":"","content":"*Raises Teacup* Cheers! Welcome to the club.<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, I wasn't against the idea of V20 being metaplot agnostic in general. The game SHOULD keep its plot optional, to make for a better sandbox for home games.<br /> <br /> But it should STILL provide such &quot;official&quot; plot material, for those who want to use it. Beckett's Jyhad Diary is probably the best form that could have taken, as it's a big menu of plots you could slot into your Chronicle. With each even giving a wide variety of branching paths, depending on how the Storyteller wants to go with them. It furthers the metaplot, but in a modular fashion that is most usable to the people buying the book.<br /> <br /> V5's approach to the metaplot, I think, was the worst of both worlds. It made it front and center, but in a way that jettisoned a lot of its most useful fixtures. (And you know Paradox saw how they messed up, as they proceeded to walk back some of its developments, like the Beckoning). If you're going to have metaplot, it needs to have utility to Storytellers. If you've got a bunch of named characters, factions, etc. it's because you expect people to USE them.<br /> <br /> The general philosophy with WoD5, especially as the games have been released, is to keep some of the trappings of the old games, but severely depopulated. Instead of the fascinating complexity and &quot;texture&quot; of Old WoD, it's severely cut down, simplified, and vacant. A &quot;slash and burn&quot; approach to WoD's established storylines. Which only serves to REMOVE options from a Storyteller's repertoire, and replace them with &quot;make it up yourselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> And if all you're expecting GMs to do with your game is make all the content themselves, you can't complain if they decide your work isn't worth buying. They're paying YOU to do the bulk of the creative work for them. If it doesn't have that, what are they buying?<br /> <br /> (That V5 makes so much of the old material non-compatible only makes it worse. You can't even backport material easily, as the rules are different in a way that precludes many old staples. Thereby, again, forcing Storytellers to do more work to adapt. At least in V20, the system itself, for better or worse, was a refinement of the old systems. You could slot old adventures, characters, or factions in with minimal conversion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T10:13:39-07:00","id":1537263,"title":"","content":"Man you are correct in abandoning V5 and the rest of the WoD5 line.<br /> Without wanting to be arrogant, I knew that the V5 had failed during the 2nd attempt to conduct a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Its rules are not consistent, Hunger dice and great in theory in practice it fails, the critical failure does not allow vampires to camouflage themselves in human society.<br /> <br /> The powers of the Disciplines are often useless or situational most of the time, few choices are solid.<br /> <br /> Character creation is limited and uncreative, predator types had great potential, but the design is weak and lazy.<br /> <br /> The character sheets should be the link to the Lore of the previous cannon but they are not enough.<br /> <br /> Blood Power and Generation was a very unsuccessful adaptation, transforming Generation into sub-levels of power was lazy.<br /> <br /> Experience points are rewards that are too slow for any gaming group to enjoy, as is the cost of increasing traits.<br /> <br /> V5's Storyline is one of the laziest things I've ever seen, they managed to ignore a rich story full of intrigue, conspiracies and mythology with several charismatic characters and incredible scenarios while ignoring the game's entire past, Beckett Jyhad Diary is the bible of Vampire the Masquerade metaplot and was completely ignored.<br /> <br /> I only have 1 wish for Djinn, Matthew Dawkins, Rose Bailey and Justin Achilli work together in Vampire The Masquerade (with rules of Vampire The Requiem 2nd base) to make the definitive Vampire rpg.<br /> <br /> If Matthew reads this please tell us what is needed for this to become a reality, and if it cannot happen what is stopping you from making this a reality through the Storyteller Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T10:50:12-07:00","id":1537266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537233#post1537233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aisling shows up in every single one of the Coteries games so she's actually gotten better than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good as she and the Follower of Set Hesha Rudhudze are the two VTM characters that I truly would use in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T13:46:07-07:00","id":1537274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5#post1537219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they weren't. V5 built on VtM's legacy in first four years or so. The first phase declared radical changes and poorly edited, if lacking something in the writing and art that previous editions had (as usual, I'm talking about VtR1.5). Then it revised itself due to unpopular demand. Onyx Path and the first version of VTMB2 combined a bit more of the status quo of V&lt;5 with the factional diversity of VtR. The Choice of Games writers did they wanted to some extent, but what they wanted was to write about the legacy, more often than not.<br /> <br /> Beyond 2021, I don't know. The Sabbat guide's lack of detail didn't inspire confidence and the topics of the later books haven't sounded that interesting to me anyway. If V5 isn't worth it, it's because of revisions that happened <i>after </i>it was created. I'm still hoping that the spirit of books like <i>Requiem for Rome</i> and <i>Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark</i> will resurface in V5 future materials, as some aspects have, but I think this toolbox approach coupled with an aversion to featuring real life cultures denies even the most talented writers the opportunities to keep giving us that soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T23:11:17-07:00","id":1537291,"title":"","content":"Ive never really been binary i ultimatly initially attempted to integrate what i liked into v5 but noticed it was easier to do the opposite. I think i was done with the edition by sabbat and w5 has confirmed that was the correct move. Overall i think the products just been consistantly mismanaged.<br /> <br /> These things cost money afterall.<br /> <br /> What has proven a real downer is the toxicity in the fanbase. The implicit disdain for sabbat players and classic werewolf for 5th ed players has been sincerly dishearetening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-13-2024, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T00:14:14-07:00","id":1537292,"title":"","content":"I like a lot of the dice mechanics of 5th edition. I adore Hunger dice, and there is a general cleanness to the dice mechanics that I like. On the other hand, the changes to the meta, and those mechanics that are built around changes to the meta, are repulsive, clearly designed to funnel us into an extremely narrow range of storytelling that boils down to parroting the typical plot of a vampire movie aimed at the normies.<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear that you are supposed to play trivial variations on the recently-turned and half-turned vampires one sees in vampire movies. You're Mina/Lucy from various Draculas, you're Michael from the &quot;Lost Boys&quot;, you're Caleb from &quot;Near Dark&quot;, etc, etc, etc. You're supposed to hate your sire, hate being a vampire, and you're supposed to destroy your sire using the subtle but potent advantages of high Humanity and low Bane-ratings. It's surprisingly inflexible. Sure, they say Tenets can be anything, but things like creating ghouls giving stains regardless of tenets, and being an Alleycat costing humanity, make it clear that tenets are really intended to be in the narrow range of the morality implied by your typical vampire movie.<br /> <br /> In short, it is a vampire-hunter game pretending to be a vampire game. Once you realize that, you also realize why they emphasize the Anarchs and have mostly destroyed the Camarilla and Sabbat: because the Anarchs are closest to not being a sect at all, and vampire movies are generally devoid of sects. They want you to worry about your sire, and maybe those few other vampires in the city that will hunt you if you kill your sire. In other words, the same thing Louis and Claudia end up worrying about.<br /> <br /> It's a very narrow, very tiny game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-14-2024, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T00:15:22-07:00","id":1537293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537291#post1537291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has proven a real downer is the toxicity in the fanbase. The implicit disdain for sabbat players and classic werewolf for 5th ed players has been sincerly dishearetening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, the Second Inquisition hurt me more than the Sabbat. I was excited and a preorder for that book because I thought:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is it! This is the book that will explain the NPCs, secret structure, and history of the Second Inquisition as well as how they operate!&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was primarily about sunlight bombs and combat stats.<br /> <br /> It was like that scene from A Christmas Story where you're told you'll shoot your eye out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T01:37:09-07:00","id":1537294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537263#post1537263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man you are correct in abandoning V5 and the rest of the WoD5 line.<br /> I only have 1 wish for Djinn, Matthew Dawkins, Rose Bailey and Justin Achilli work together in Vampire The Masquerade (with rules of Vampire The Requiem 2nd base) to make the definitive Vampire rpg.<br /> <br /> If Matthew reads this please tell us what is needed for this to become a reality, and if it cannot happen what is stopping you from making this a reality through the Storyteller Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>The djinn came to me in the night and told me of your plea. My response is this: <br /> <br /> With respect, no thank you. I worked for a long time on Vampire and while I may take a contract on a book, board game, or video game if it's offered to me, I'm not actively seeking work for the World of Darkness. Games like The World Below, They Came From, and Curseborne (which you should really be looking up if you're a World of Darkness fan) are what creatively inspire me at this point, and are what I'm actively working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T04:32:55-07:00","id":1537299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537293#post1537293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, the Second Inquisition hurt me more than the Sabbat. I was excited and a preorder for that book because I thought:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is it! This is the book that will explain the NPCs, secret structure, and history of the Second Inquisition as well as how they operate!&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was primarily about sunlight bombs and combat stats.<br /> <br /> It was like that scene from A Christmas Story where you're told you'll shoot your eye out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat didnt really 'hurt' me but it sort of showed me the way the wind was blowing and decided to avoid investment fallacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T05:08:53-07:00","id":1537302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537294#post1537294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The djinn came to me in the night and told me of your plea. My response is this:<br /> <br /> With respect, no thank you. I worked for a long time on Vampire and while I may take a contract on a book, board game, or video game if it's offered to me, I'm not actively seeking work for the World of Darkness. Games like The World Below, They Came From, and Curseborne (which you should really be looking up if you're a World of Darkness fan) are what creatively inspire me at this point, and are what I'm actively working on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very intrigued by Curseborne now and I am very curious about what's coming out for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T05:15:51-07:00","id":1537337,"title":"","content":"Well, I for one welcome you into the light. Its a sad state of affairs but holding on to what can only disapoint you time and again can only lead to more disapointment. I am glad you're out of that circle and wish you a ton of fun playing the game in a healthier way.<br /> <br /> I'm sure a lot of folks genuinely love X5 but I'm also sure a lot of people are in denial loke you were and its not helping anyone. Least of all those players. PDX can still fix this and course correct but they won't do that so long as they think this is working and its what people want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3822-yiodan","name":"Yiodan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T09:42:34-07:00","id":1537343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537237#post1537237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry, actually, as I know how much you were invested on it.<br /> <br /> <b>V20 is the way to go for any sort of continuation of the old setting, and Requiem 2nd is a far better new setting. Trying to be both and none at the same time was a bad idea for V5.</b><br /> <br /> All we can do now is to hope that they someday notice the lines they can still invest in and let OPP do its job with them in peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>[emphasis mine]<br /> <br /> I think this puts it perfectly. <br /> <br /> V5 never managed to catch my curiosity. For me it's either VDA20/VtM20, or Chronicles of Darkness, which is what I am looking into atm (about to narrate my first campaign in general, going for Mummy the Curse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T12:47:56-07:00","id":1537348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yiodan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537337#post1537337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I for one welcome you into the light. Its a sad state of affairs but holding on to what can only disapoint you time and again can only lead to more disapointment. I am glad you're out of that circle and wish you a ton of fun playing the game in a healthier way.<br /> <br /> I'm sure a lot of folks genuinely love X5 but I'm also sure a lot of people are in denial loke you were and its not helping anyone. Least of all those players. PDX can still fix this and course correct but they won't do that so long as they think this is working and its what people want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fundamentally, I think there was a change behind the scenes that must have happened or there was a shift in priorities somewhere. For me, in retrospect, I was never a fan of V5 so much as I was a fan of what OPP and certain authots (MD for example in THE CAMARILLA) did with the setting. I kind of have to wonder how much of it was them, to quote Blade, iceskating uphill and trying to save as much of the old WOD as possible, though.<br /> <br /> The Fall of London, Chicago books, and Cults of the Blood Gods books struck a good balance between old material and new material. It felt like a genuine continuation of the Old Line and that they were respecting the necessary struggle between getting new players involved in the game while attracting the old ones.<br /> <br /> The new books just don't feel that way and seem actively hostile to the old setting and characters. The loresheets felt like a nod in the right direction but even they are now disappearing from the backs of the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T17:57:47-07:00","id":1537373,"title":"","content":"V5 could have been its own thing if it went full dive in the Gehenna instead of trying to be the same game. It could be a new game with roots in the same lore.<br /> <br /> The moment they decided they would starve V20 and VtR to have only V5, and to ignore things like BJD, I think the writing was already on the wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T18:04:04-07:00","id":1537374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537373#post1537373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 could have been its own thing if it went full dive in the Gehenna instead of trying to be the same game. It could be a new game with roots in the same lore.<br /> <br /> The moment they decided they would starve V20 and VtR to have only V5, and to ignore things like BJD, I think the writing was already on the wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not V:TM if it's Gehenna and really I just wanted a setting updated for the Post-9/11 and Financial Crash world.<br /> <br /> OPP did several fantastic supplements for V5.<br /> <br /> CBN, The Chicago Folios, LTTSRR, Blood Cults, Trail of Bone and Ashes, and Children of the Blood. That's a substantial chunk of the line.<br /> <br /> The other spin off material like the web streams and visual novels also struck a good balance. It was easy to delude yourself into believing Legacy was respected rather than simply something they didn't think &quot;counted.&quot;<br /> <br /> Winter's Teeth was fantastic.<br /> <br /> It's really impressive how much they had to reverse course on all this to try to get rid of what people wanted to know more about. Why bother introducing so many mysteries like the events at Vienna, Alamut, and things like Lasombra joining the Camarilla or Setites joining the Anarchs if you're not going to follow up on them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T19:34:29-07:00","id":1537378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537374#post1537374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not V:TM if it's Gehenna.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but V5 is Gehenna.<br /> <br /> As much as they tried to downplay it and backpedal a lot of things, V5 is Gehenna, and that's why they should have kept investing in V20 in parallel, as two storylines that diverged under the plot power of the Red Star.<br /> <br /> The problem is that V5 tried to be many things, but those things are irreconcilable. Two of those things, being a new setting and being the continuation of legacy, we had good lines already doing. Lines that could do wonders with the money they were denied.<br /> <br /> One third thing they proposed right off the bat to be: the continuation of the plot picking from Time of Judgement.<br /> <br /> Back in the day, if they had decided to pick from BJD and not streamline the intended modes of play, maybe V5 could have been a new edition to V20. But since in the end that was never the intention, the next best way for V5 to thrive is to embrace itself and be its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T01:48:37-07:00","id":1537386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537374#post1537374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's really impressive how much they had to reverse course on all this to try to get rid of what people wanted to know more about. Why bother introducing so many mysteries like the events at Vienna, Alamut, and things like Lasombra joining the Camarilla or Setites joining the Anarchs if you're not going to follow up on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the objective is adjustments to setting play rather than a meaningful story. The lasombra defection is because their's a group of people who want to play lasombra outside Sabbat rather than as a logical progression of events and so forth, aside from stretching credibility their isn't any actual interest in the fallout that would occur because that's not the point. By my estimation the vtm setting is currently experiencing the equivalent of ongoing nuclear war in terms of social upheaval but for some reason the setting looks very similar to vtm circa 95 because the objective is to try and make a setting an specific idea of how current writters think it should look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-15-2024, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T06:13:59-07:00","id":1537392,"title":"","content":"When V5 first came out I quite liked it, as someone who was never old enough to play VTM but dived into VTR, I actually liked how it borrowed elements from both. I also enjoyed the Camarilla and Anarch books and you can see clearly the passion and themes that they're trying to put forward their. The books feel like work of arts, which doesn't help their layout granted but did help to get me into the feeling of what those games were doing.<br /> <br /> After that,the Renegade books have just been more game books than anything. A collection of generic stats I'd expect in an old 3.5 book with some generic advice you can apply to your home setting. That's not what I wanted from VTM, I wanted the world of Masquerade, the world of Bloodlines etc that I loved and wanted to expereince.<br /> <br /> For me W5 was the real turning point, reading the Tribes and how watered down they were, there's literally no reason to have that many tribes or even be a part of the tribe now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28524-impulsive93","name":"Impulsive93","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T08:37:46-07:00","id":1537400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537373#post1537373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 could have been its own thing if it went full dive in the Gehenna instead of trying to be the same game. It could be a new game with roots in the same lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T11:44:26-07:00","id":1537415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537348#post1537348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fundamentally, I think there was a change behind the scenes that must have happened or there was a shift in priorities somewhere. For me, in retrospect, I was never a fan of V5 so much as I was a fan of what OPP and certain authots (MD for example in THE CAMARILLA) did with the setting. I kind of have to wonder how much of it was them, to quote Blade, iceskating uphill and trying to save as much of the old WOD as possible, though.<br /> <br /> The Fall of London, Chicago books, and Cults of the Blood Gods books struck a good balance between old material and new material. It felt like a genuine continuation of the Old Line and that they were respecting the necessary struggle between getting new players involved in the game while attracting the old ones.<br /> <br /> The new books just don't feel that way and seem actively hostile to the old setting and characters. The loresheets felt like a nod in the right direction but even they are now disappearing from the backs of the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still play V5. but I haven't bought most of the new books. (I bought Bloodstained Love because I think it's an interesting concept and a lot of people were very dismissive of it.) This is mostly due to as you said: There's this odd hostility and dismissiveness for lore. From the Player's Guide telling you no one cares about your loresheets but you, the DoC loresheet and Gargoyle reference that feel like they were thrown out so older fans would stop talking, and the general way I speak to some V5 fans. They often seem...upset that you like/want old lore. I'm a newer player, but even I get vitriol for saying I like legacy material. I've never experienced this in any other community, and as much as I hear about &quot;grognards&quot;, it's usually among them I'm being told what I enjoy makes me a miscreant. It is quite off-putting. I love all the books you mention here, and even though Fall of London is a mess, it's an interesting mess. I'd rather have something with a weird idea that's interesting than something safe and boring.<br /> <br /> There was definitely a shift in regards of what they wanted with the lore and metaplot. Tis sad, but I'm just reading through old books now for ideas and enjoyment. And I do have all the V5 Onyx Path books. Sorry your love has been crushed, I've watched you champion this edition for years, and I've seen you chatting around elsewhere. To a new player who has similar feelings: Ya ain't alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27814-agornitha","user":"Agornitha","date":". 06-15-2024, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27814-agornitha","name":"Agornitha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27814_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T00:51:27-07:00","id":1537468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agornitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537415#post1537415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never experienced this in any other community, and as much as I hear about &quot;grognards&quot;, it's usually among them I'm being told what I enjoy makes me a miscreant.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The weird part is if you look at historic attitudes in the fandom its clear the dislike of deeper lore, obsession with specific style of play and disdain for certain aspects of the fandom is actually an issue as far back as at least the early 00's. V5 is actually the edition were the grognards got what they wanted and see that as affirimitive of their (often toxic) outlooks. Although i do think they missed the mark when they think the company is explicitly catering to their outlook when its more product mismanagement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-16-2024, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T03:08:32-07:00","id":1537476,"title":"","content":"I remember having this conversation with a V5 fanatic:<br /> <br /> - V5 is a mature game because you play in a real and adult setting. It isn't like those nerds who play DnD or other fantasy games. Woah, they're so childish\u00a1\u00a1<br /> <br /> Me: Err Do you know that WoD is Urban fantasy? I mean, Vampires doesn't exist, mages neither. All of them are fantasy creature... It's fantasy like DnD. Maybe with some differences but they're part of the same genre. (I'm sure that I killed a Changeling with the last statement)<br /> <br /> -Oh\u00a1 Hmmm but it's another fantasy, you know. It's different. It's MaTuRe\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1\u00a1<br /> <br /> I still love WoD games, they have a very special place in my heart. But for people like this, they're starting to become a guilty pleasure. Yeah, I really love personal horror and drama. I love a serious game and a setting based in the real world. But I love the weirdness of Wod, I love the silly aspects of the splats too. I love the use of fantasy elements when it fits, because they're fantasy/horror games at the end of the day. Because you're Wod character kills children that doesn't make you more mature. But a ray of hope or sillynes can make a whole session more adult.<br /> <br /> I saw pretty stupid things like &quot;You can't play a lupus garou because you wouldn't be a wolf in real life&quot; (they did the same treatment to disabled and native american characters) . Also, it kills me the &quot;V5 is more realistic in their treatment of vampires&quot; (oh yeah, you know so many vampires in real life, right?) or &quot;if you play Sabbat, you need mental assistance. WoD isn't the place to play grey or straight villains characters&quot;. Also they take Wod games as a form to understand the world, for them, Wod has to reflect exactly the real life, so no fantasy. I was abused for these kind of people, they hurted me and my friends. And they're one of the most amoral people that I ever know in my life. I could say more and more, but I'm pretty tired of all this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T04:12:30-07:00","id":1537477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5#post1537219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 should have been the death blow to my idealism with the hints that W:TA 1-20 were now non-canon and irreconcilable but I stubbornly denied what was in front of my face. I should have known you can only trust people with a genuine love of the material. I don't get that feeling outside of the livestream games.<br /> <br /> So from now on, it'll just be cherishing what OPP has already made and Storyteller's Vault material.<br /> <br /> You guys were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah please give me more examples where it is said the W5 is handling previous canon like Disney SW. On the CoG Forums they do not want to believe it, heavily disagreeing with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T06:57:58-07:00","id":1537485,"title":"","content":"I was never a fan of 5th Edition, starting from that atrocious magazine style V5 core book. I think I gave up after the Second Inquisition book. I wanted to know how previously ineffectual groups like SAD, CIA (remember Bob? The only CIA agent who had an inkling of supernatural and was considered senile old men.) etc. become the Inquisition but saw BS. I lost hope on 5th Edition after W5 &quot;re-imagining&quot;.<br /> <br /> I wish you good luck. It is hard being old fan of a setting, whose current owner just keeps disregarding you to chase the &quot;wider audience&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T09:38:20-07:00","id":1537498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537468#post1537468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The weird part is if you look at historic attitudes in the fandom its clear the dislike of deeper lore, obsession with specific style of play and disdain for certain aspects of the fandom is actually an issue as far back as at least the early 00's. V5 is actually the edition were the grognards got what they wanted and see that as affirimitive of their (often toxic) outlooks. Although i do think they missed the mark when they think the company is explicitly catering to their outlook when its more product mismanagement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it is as old as 1st Edition, way back to 1991. Since always WoD has catered to a group of mostly young people with an obsession for a certain style of play for being theoretically mature and disdain/hate for badwrongfun. <br /> <br /> In fact, many here were those types or somewhat similar when we got to the game. Some still are, even if not liking V5. This is a fact about WoD we also have to come to terms with, and there have always been authors who do encourage such stupidity.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-16T10:01:27-07:00","id":1537501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537477#post1537477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah please give me more examples where it is said the W5 is handling previous canon like Disney SW. On the CoG Forums they do not want to believe it, heavily disagreeing with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what this means but they've said that it is a soft reboot rather than a continuation.<br /> <br /> That anything previously established was no longer necessarily canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537498#post1537498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it is as old as 1st Edition, way back to 1991. Since always WoD has catered to a group of mostly young people with an obsession for a certain style of play for being theoretically mature and disdain/hate for badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> In fact, many here were those types or somewhat similar when we got to the game. Some still are, even if not liking V5. This is a fact about WoD we also have to come to terms with, and there have always been authors who do encourage such stupidity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Honestly, I don't think V5 caters to the grognard crowd very much at all. I'm definitely one of the oriinal &quot;Mark Rein Hagen did it best&quot; crowd and frankly while they talked a good game, V5 is very much against a lot of the themes of V1. This isn't a 100% condemnation and different publishers and writers did different things with V5, some better than others, but the things that V1 did can be summarized in five bullet points.<br /> <br /> * Gothic Romance<br /> * Personal Horror<br /> * Punk sensibilities<br /> * Strong NPC characterization<br /> * Intertwined NPCs<br /> <br /> V5 claimed to have made the Anarchs big again but for the life of me, I'm not sure what the Anarchs are about in the setting any more than other games.\u200b The Punk sensibility of overthrowing the man and opposing his tyranny is almost absent because the Anarchs are not just shown to be hypocrites but every bit as bad as the Camarilla. The strong NPC characterizations are less so because outside of the OPP books, there's almost no focus on NPCs. The Gothic Romance and beauty of Kindred life is utterly absent as well.<br /> <br /> Bloodstained Love had some of what I was looking for there but its focus on bleed was terrible because, really, I feel that a lot of Western storytellers and gamers are less actors than authors. Its not about BEING your character so much as writing a story FOR your characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2024, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T09:14:26-07:00","id":1537562,"title":"","content":"As someone who was here when you first started (back then with this account: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\">Crytash</a>), I must say that it is sad to see you came to dislike the game of V5. I never really liked it, so with you, at least, I knew that some people genuinely preferred it over either Revised or V20. That said, you were also really annoying to me with the way you cheerleadered the game.<br /> <br /> Emotionally, I was quite invested in the older game lines, but now and in the end, I can only say &quot;/shrug&quot;. It might be a privileged viewpoint, but in the end, I just stopped discussing the game and I kind of lost track of you. From time to time, I would come back to this forum and see you as a mod, etc. and feel a sense of weltschmerz, a melancholy realization that things have irrevocably changed. The vibrancy and passion of the old debates, the intense involvement in the storylines, all seem like distant memories now. It\u2019s as if a chapter has closed, not just in the game but in our collective experience as a community.<br /> <br /> The transition from V5 enthusiasm to a resigned acceptance of V20 might mirror a broader shift in how the community engages with WoD. You are not the only die hard V5 person i have seen switching recently. The excitement that once surrounded new releases and updates has given way to a more subdued, perhaps cynical, outlook. You guys and gals used to argue fiercely over the minutiae of the lore and mechanics, but now it seems like the fire has dimmed. It\u2019s a strange, bittersweet evolution\u2014part of growing up, i guess. Eh, enough with all the sadness here a video to cheer you up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_dUmDBfp6k\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_dUmDBfp6k\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_dUmDBfp6k </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_dUmDBfp6k\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_dUmDBfp6k </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T10:18:08-07:00","id":1537565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537562#post1537562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who was here when you first started (back then with this account: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\">Crytash</a>), I must say that it is sad to see you came to dislike the game of V5. I never really liked it, so with you, at least, I knew that some people genuinely preferred it over either Revised or V20. That said, you were also really annoying to me with the way you cheerleadered the game.<br /> <br /> Emotionally, I was quite invested in the older game lines, but now and in the end, I can only say &quot;/shrug&quot;. It might be a privileged viewpoint, but in the end, I just stopped discussing the game and I kind of lost track of you. From time to time, I would come back to this forum and see you as a mod, etc. and feel a sense of weltschmerz, a melancholy realization that things have irrevocably changed. The vibrancy and passion of the old debates, the intense involvement in the storylines, all seem like distant memories now. It\u2019s as if a chapter has closed, not just in the game but in our collective experience as a community.<br /> <br /> The transition from V5 enthusiasm to a resigned acceptance of V20 might mirror a broader shift in how the community engages with WoD. You are not the only die hard V5 person i have seen switching recently. The excitement that once surrounded new releases and updates has given way to a more subdued, perhaps cynical, outlook. You guys and gals used to argue fiercely over the minutiae of the lore and mechanics, but now it seems like the fire has dimmed. It\u2019s a strange, bittersweet evolution\u2014part of growing up, i guess. Eh, enough with all the sadness here a video to cheer you up:</div> </div> </div> </div>Your call.<br /> <br /> But for me, the enthusiasm is because it feels like the game fundamentally stopped caring about what mattered most not that it was me somehow having a revelation of what it always was.<br /> <br /> In truth, the creators never stopped caring but the people deciding what was coming out probably never did care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T12:37:32-07:00","id":1537571,"title":"","content":"Fan apathy is the worse thing to see in the entertainment industry. We have been disappointed so many times that we expect whatever is coming down the pike to be lackluster at best or awful at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T13:08:26-07:00","id":1537580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537501#post1537501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what this means but they've said that it is a soft reboot rather than a continuation.<br /> <br /> That anything previously established was no longer necessarily canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't think V5 caters to the grognard crowd very much at all. I'm definitely one of the oriinal &quot;Mark Rein Hagen did it best&quot; crowd and frankly while they talked a good game, V5 is very much against a lot of the themes of V1. This isn't a 100% condemnation and different publishers and writers did different things with V5, some better than others, but the things that V1 did can be summarized in five bullet points.<br /> <br /> * Gothic Romance<br /> * Personal Horror<br /> * Punk sensibilities<br /> * Strong NPC characterization<br /> * Intertwined NPCs<br /> <br /> V5 claimed to have made the Anarchs big again but for the life of me, I'm not sure what the Anarchs are about in the setting any more than other games. The Punk sensibility of overthrowing the man and opposing his tyranny is almost absent because the Anarchs are not just shown to be hypocrites but every bit as bad as the Camarilla. The strong NPC characterizations are less so because outside of the OPP books, there's almost no focus on NPCs. The Gothic Romance and beauty of Kindred life is utterly absent as well.<br /> <br /> Bloodstained Love had some of what I was looking for there but its focus on bleed was terrible because, really, I feel that a lot of Western storytellers and gamers are less actors than authors. Its not about BEING your character so much as writing a story FOR your characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vtm grognards have always been weird, they've latched onto an idealized version of VTM which was never really universal hyper focused on personal horror and explicitly rejecting alternative explorations of the setting (action orientated games, paths, Sabbat etc) as well as a series of arbitrary complaints (no unique disciplines, I don't like the clans have lore which makes certain play choices difficult, true black hand etc). V5 kinda accidentally ascribes to a lot of their requests such as humanity or the downplaying of clan identity and they mistake that for affirmation. the important trait of vtm grognards is not only do they have specific excepectations of the game but object to deviation in other players from this.<br /> <br /> It is not enough that you play the game the way it's 'supposed' to be others must not be allowed to play it 'wrong' and they mistake paradox's policies for agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-17-2024, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T20:31:23-07:00","id":1537599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537571#post1537571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fan apathy is the worse thing to see in the entertainment industry. We have been disappointed so many times that we expect whatever is coming down the pike to be lackluster at best or awful at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically where I am with Paradox-White Wolf these days. I expect nothing and yet somehow I still end up being a bit disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T09:09:29-07:00","id":1537619,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, it is kind if sobering that you've given up o the products. The only two people ive encountered with your enthusiasm for it are either respectively so in lockstep with company outlooks that i suspect they're actually a designer or corporate community plant or with the other one, psychotic. Youre the only guy seemed nornal in your enthusiasm. It reflects badly they couldnt keep you interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-18-2024, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T10:49:46-07:00","id":1537625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537565#post1537565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your call.<br /> <br /> But for me, the enthusiasm is because it feels like the game fundamentally stopped caring about what mattered most not that it was me somehow having a revelation of what it always was.<br /> <br /> In truth, the creators never stopped caring but the people deciding what was coming out probably never did care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve reflected on my previous response and realize it may have come across as harsh. If the game has indeed changed in a way that impacts you deeply and you it lost that part, I understand how that could feel quite depressing and leave you feeling empty. Whatever direction you choose to take from here (you said you want to play V20, but no one knows if that scratchesd the same itch for you), please remember to take care of yourself. Nothing quite as frustrating than trying to like sth and not feeling it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T15:43:43-07:00","id":1537664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537619#post1537619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it, it is kind if sobering that you've given up o the products. The only two people ive encountered with your enthusiasm for it are either respectively so in lockstep with company outlooks that i suspect they're actually a designer or corporate community plant or with the other one, psychotic. Youre the only guy seemed nornal in your enthusiasm. It reflects badly they couldnt keep you interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, this is a very familiar feeling because it's basically the same one that I had for THE FORCE AWAKENS as I was incredibly interested in the world-building and mysteries that had been set up. The Gehenna War, the fate of the Sabbat, the fate of Signature NPCs, and the mysteries of things like, &quot;Why did Theo Bell kill Hardelstadt?&quot; &quot;What is the forces behind the Second Inquisition&quot;. &quot;What is the cause of the Beckoning?&quot;, &quot;Is Lucita dead?&quot;, and &quot;What was the Vermillion Wedding's repercussions?&quot;, &quot;How will the Anarchs develop?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, I was in full binge watch prestige TV mode and the results ended up being the increasing realization that either only certain creators were actually interested in exploring these questions or they weren't actually questions that had answers. They created the mysteries without ever actually intending to answer them. THE LAST JEDI really annoyed me as a movie but it wasn't until THE RISE OF SKYWALKER that I realized they were just making it up as they went along and didn't have any actual plan.<br /> <br /> I mentioned THE SECOND INQUISITION book disappointed me more than THE SABBAT book and I think that can be summarized in the realization the Second Inquisition didn't have any history, NPCs, cause and effect, or personality to it beyond, &quot;They will come and fuck up the vampires.&quot; This is a SHARP contrast to two of my all time favorite WOD supplements: PROJECT TWILIGHT and THE GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY.<br /> <br /> Project: Twilight detailed the SAD department extensively with NPCs that represented competiting factions, goals, ideologies, and operating procedures. The Guide to the Technocracy didn't have any NPCs but it had loads and loads of personality. You could side with the Union but also understand if the ST wanted to treat them as a bunch of fascist murderers. Both sides were represented and were consistent. It also was almost entirely removed from the previous depiction of the SAD, Inquisition, and NSA.<br /> <br /> I wanted books full of mysteries and answers and got....stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T19:53:04-07:00","id":1537670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537226#post1537226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well only if you want to discuss V5. LIke I said, V20 is the last defending outpost of lore and history for the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to take issue with that, sort of. M20 definitely has its share of lore and history. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T21:18:27-07:00","id":1537674,"title":"","content":"As for the OP, take want you like from WODFive and enjoy your games. My friends aren't comfortable with CoD, but, when I run OG, Requiem, I'm using variable sunlight-damage rules from CoD. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537664#post1537664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mentioned THE SECOND INQUISITION book disappointed me more than THE SABBAT book and I think that can be summarized in the realization the Second Inquisition didn't have any history, NPCs, cause and effect, or personality to it beyond, &quot;They will come and fuck up the vampires.&quot; . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Krud, I think I got that book used; haven't read it. I did enjoy Dark Age: Inquisition (and HH) though, even though, it was hard to follow. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T21:24:47-07:00","id":1537675,"title":"","content":"I said from day one that V5 sucks and everything connected to the setting and style of V5 is fundamentally tainted to an irredeemable agree. But I was one of V5's biggest haters even before it came out. I did get the corebook to try and give it a fair shake and I regretted it. Seeing even more of the other setting changes in later books, it honestly disgusted me even further.<br /> <br /> The moment they announced they were outright fully abandoning the metaplot-agnostic approach of V20, I knew it was going to be a shitshow, at least for me. <br /> <br /> I know you and me will never agree on metaplot, but I sympathize with you on being soured by V5, Mr. Phipps. Even if it is for opposite reasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T23:38:10-07:00","id":1537678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537675#post1537675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said from day one that V5 sucks and everything connected to the setting and style of V5 is fundamentally tainted to an irredeemable agree. But I was one of V5's biggest haters even before it came out. I did get the corebook to try and give it a fair shake and I regretted it. Seeing even more of the other setting changes in later books, it honestly disgusted me even further.<br /> <br /> The moment they announced they were outright fully abandoning the metaplot-agnostic approach of V20, I knew it was going to be a shitshow, at least for me.<br /> <br /> I know you and me will never agree on metaplot, but I sympathize with you on being soured by V5, Mr. Phipps. Even if it is for opposite reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hilariously, what's killed it is the fact they're adopting a metaplot agnostic setting. I'm like, &quot;Fuck it, what's the point now?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pick a lane, guys.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T04:33:10-07:00","id":1537683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537678#post1537678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, hilariously, what's killed it is the fact they're adopting a metaplot agnostic setting. I'm like, &quot;Fuck it, what's the point now?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pick a lane, guys.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, they're not really adopting a metaplot agnostic setting. They're still keeping all the setting changes from before instead of doing a hard retcon of them.<br /> <br /> If you want a true metaplot-agnostic setting, go for V20. <br /> <br /> V20 is ten times better than V5, IMHO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:29:34-07:00","id":1537693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537683#post1537683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then, they're not really adopting a metaplot agnostic setting. They're still keeping all the setting changes from before instead of doing a hard retcon of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are keeping a default setting from the start ala Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want a true metaplot-agnostic setting, go for V20.<br /> <br /> V20 is ten times better than V5, IMHO </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, they moved away from that at the end and BJD was the greatest of the books written for V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T06:53:48-07:00","id":1537702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5#post1537219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know no one will care</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda care because I fairly recently read your review of W5 on reddit and greatly appreciated it.<br /> <br /> Granted, I stay on my position of not buying the book but I found the reading honest and endearing.<br /> I especially liked the part where you worded what you always saw as a good premise of WtA, which was akin to &quot;basically the Garou were presented as a sledgehammer that treated every problem in the last 20000 years as a nail&quot;<br /> <br /> I liked reading it, and it pushed me to get my hands back on a WtA scenario that I've been working on for years to publish on the vault.<br /> It also prompted me to a mad project (that I'm sure I'll never complete) about a 13 tribes chronicle set in each decade from 1900 onward and in each decade the players play as a single tribe pack.<br /> But yeah, it mostly pushed me further back on the 20th anniversary stuff.<br /> So I completely get where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> WoD5 is a missed opportunity, because I liked the streamlined mechanics and the hunger dice is a nice idea and if it were a bit less punishing would be more fun.<br /> My only interest in WoD5 now is a possible WtO new 'edition'. Not for the setting but for more streamlined rules that I could use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T10:18:18-07:00","id":1537714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537693#post1537693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they are keeping a default setting from the start ala Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thankfully, they moved away from that at the end and BJD was the greatest of the books written for V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yeah, but the default setting still has a lot of changes. Even the V5 corebook's metaplot changes were too much,<br /> <br /> 2. That's what I didn't like about V20. I hated BJD and the attempt at resuming metaplot. I prefer the setting of early 2e for VTM, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> But again, to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 06-20-2024, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T13:07:09-07:00","id":1537725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537664#post1537664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, this is a very familiar feeling because it's basically the same one that I had for THE FORCE AWAKENS as I was incredibly interested in the world-building and mysteries that had been set up. The Gehenna War, the fate of the Sabbat, the fate of Signature NPCs, and the mysteries of things like, &quot;Why did Theo Bell kill Hardelstadt?&quot; &quot;What is the forces behind the Second Inquisition&quot;. &quot;What is the cause of the Beckoning?&quot;, &quot;Is Lucita dead?&quot;, and &quot;What was the Vermillion Wedding's repercussions?&quot;, &quot;How will the Anarchs develop?&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, I was in full binge watch prestige TV mode and the results ended up being the increasing realization that either only certain creators were actually interested in exploring these questions or they weren't actually questions that had answers. They created the mysteries without ever actually intending to answer them. THE LAST JEDI really annoyed me as a movie but it wasn't until THE RISE OF SKYWALKER that I realized they were just making it up as they went along and didn't have any actual plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit us WoD5 critics kind of clocked to at the start: all these setting changes were not made to add more stories, but to SUBTRACT existing ones. They were written to sweep away NPCs and factions from the old continuity, so V5's writers would never need to deal with them ever again.<br /> <br /> They were never meant to be mysteries. They were excuses. Excuses for why the setting is suddenly a huge blank slate.<br /> <br /> At least V20's &quot;Metaplot Agnostic&quot; approach didn't invalidate the old fixtures. It just made them optional. And it still took time to make its own plot as the edition went on, like with the Montmartre Pact or BJD. They knew the metaplot had value, even if it shouldn't be a shackle around the wrists of Storytellers.<br /> <br /> V5's &quot;mysteries&quot; were nothing of the sort, because they were never meant to be. All they existed to do was wipe the slate clean. And then V5's writers proceeded to replace it with basically nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mentioned THE SECOND INQUISITION book disappointed me more than THE SABBAT book and I think that can be summarized in the realization the Second Inquisition didn't have any history, NPCs, cause and effect, or personality to it beyond, &quot;They will come and fuck up the vampires.&quot; This is a SHARP contrast to two of my all time favorite WOD supplements: PROJECT TWILIGHT and THE GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY.<br /> <br /> Project: Twilight detailed the SAD department extensively with NPCs that represented competiting factions, goals, ideologies, and operating procedures. The Guide to the Technocracy didn't have any NPCs but it had loads and loads of personality. You could side with the Union but also understand if the ST wanted to treat them as a bunch of fascist murderers. Both sides were represented and were consistent. It also was almost entirely removed from the previous depiction of the SAD, Inquisition, and NSA.<br /> <br /> I wanted books full of mysteries and answers and got....stats. </div> </div> </div>The Second Inquisition is a continuation of my point above. V5's writers plainly did not conceptualize hunter orgs like this as potential protagonists of their own stories. (Something made depressingly obvious by H5's open, textual, seething contempt for hunter orgs). The SI was intended exclusively as a Vampire-facing fixture. An antagonist faction that existed to hammer Kindred down when they got too uppity, and to enforce greater levels of secrecy and insularity. Especially on the part of the Camarilla, which V5's designers didn't want players acting within anymore. (It's the same reason why the Sabbat got blown up; the Gehenna Wars are not playable, because V5 did not want people playing Sabbat characters).<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, SAD and other groups got detailed write-ups, internal factions, and NPCs, because they were meant to be playable. Now the SI are baddies thrown at VtM players if they deviate from the street-level play V5's was meant for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T17:57:06-07:00","id":1537735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537599#post1537599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's basically where I am with Paradox-White Wolf these days. I expect nothing and yet somehow I still end up being a bit disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the last decade or so has been a let down for good entertainment in most genre and I have been going for stuff that is indie or not mainstream big budget productions to find a sense of escapism that I crave when I'm not working or dealing with personal issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:34:21-07:00","id":1537741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537725#post1537725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's &quot;mysteries&quot; were nothing of the sort, because they were never meant to be. All they existed to do was wipe the slate clean. And then V5's writers proceeded to replace it with basically nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when V5 first released, even though I was fairly tepid towards it overall, I was looking forward to some of the metaplot mysteries that the game had put forward. What is the Beckoning? What happened at the Family Reunion? What exactly is the nature of the Ministry/Followers of Set split? I've seen a lot of different interpretations on that, from the Ministry just being a rebranding, to the Ministry tossing Set out and replacing the idea of Set with worshipping numerous different figures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:40:26-07:00","id":1537742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537725#post1537725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit us WoD5 critics kind of clocked to at the start: all these setting changes were not made to add more stories, but to SUBTRACT existing ones. They were written to sweep away NPCs and factions from the old continuity, so V5's writers would never need to deal with them ever again.<br /> <br /> They were never meant to be mysteries. They were excuses. Excuses for why the setting is suddenly a huge blank slate.<br /> <br /> At least V20's &quot;Metaplot Agnostic&quot; approach didn't invalidate the old fixtures. It just made them optional. And it still took time to make its own plot as the edition went on, like with the Montmartre Pact or BJD. They knew the metaplot had value, even if it shouldn't be a shackle around the wrists of Storytellers.<br /> <br /> V5's &quot;mysteries&quot; were nothing of the sort, because they were never meant to be. All they existed to do was wipe the slate clean. And then V5's writers proceeded to replace it with basically nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the metaplot agnostic approach of V20 effectively &quot;reset the clock&quot; with all of the events in the setting from the Clan Novels to the Kuei Jin invasion to other events in the books. Which invalidated a very large chunk of supplements. This isn't always a bad thing and plenty of people liked it but a lot of things like the Assamites, Ravnos, Salubri Antitribu, and thin Bloods were heavily tied to the advancing metaplot.<br /> <br /> I can't dispute the idea that Paradox Interactive didn't actually have a plan for the things they created, though. The Beckoning and gehenna War seem to have been rewritten mulitple times behind the scenes and the Sabbat were transformed multiple times. They also weirdly had an aversion to being clear about some things.<br /> <br /> Like, why NOT just say, &quot;The Kuei Jin are non-canon now and we're never going to address them.&quot; It would have saved some trouble, I think and I generally approve of that decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Second Inquisition is a continuation of my point above. V5's writers plainly did not conceptualize hunter orgs like this as potential protagonists of their own stories. (Something made depressingly obvious by H5's open, textual, seething contempt for hunter orgs). The SI was intended exclusively as a Vampire-facing fixture. An antagonist faction that existed to hammer Kindred down when they got too uppity, and to enforce greater levels of secrecy and insularity. Especially on the part of the Camarilla, which V5's designers didn't want players acting within anymore. (It's the same reason why the Sabbat got blown up; the Gehenna Wars are not playable, because V5 did not want people playing Sabbat characters).<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, SAD and other groups got detailed write-ups, internal factions, and NPCs, because they were meant to be playable. Now the SI are baddies thrown at VtM players if they deviate from the street-level play V5's was meant for. </div> </div> </div>I come from a very different school of VTM thought that you don't NEED for a faction to be playable to want them to be as detailed as player characters. Chicago by Night wrote up the antagonists the same way they would player characters with all the personality, motivations, and goals needed because that was inherently more interesting and effective. Lodin may have been a piece of shit no one was expected to like or work with but the write-up for him but damn if I didn't know what made him tick.<br /> <br /> Which made him a much better villain when I did use him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537741#post1537741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, when V5 first released, even though I was fairly tepid towards it overall, I was looking forward to some of the metaplot mysteries that the game had put forward. What is the Beckoning? What happened at the Family Reunion? What exactly is the nature of the Ministry/Followers of Set split? <b>I've seen a lot of different interpretations on that, from the Ministry just being a rebranding, to the Ministry tossing Set out and replacing the idea of Set with worshipping numerous different figures</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I get the impression that it fell upon (a) certain author(s) with OPP to fill in that gap and others. Not going to say it outright that I don't think Paradox cared beyond, &quot;oh yeah, they're Anarchs now.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the OPP idea of an ideological split along &quot;god of darkness&quot; ecumenist polytheism and monotheistic orthodox Typhonism was the best one of them by far and unsurprisingly what they were hinting at in BJD.<br /> <br /> CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS really felt like trying to save as much as possible while being lore friendly to new players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-20-2024, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T20:10:02-07:00","id":1537745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537742#post1537742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression that it fell upon (a) certain author(s) with OPP to fill in that gap and others. Not going to say it outright that I don't think Paradox cared beyond, &quot;oh yeah, they're Anarchs now.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the OPP idea of an ideological split along &quot;god of darkness&quot; ecumenist polytheism and monotheistic orthodox Typhonism was the best one of them by far and unsurprisingly what they were hinting at in BJD.<br /> <br /> CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS really felt like trying to save as much as possible while being lore friendly to new players.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Followers were always one of my favorite clans in theory, but I always felt disappointed that the clan of religious fanatics didn't have schisms, fights over interpretation, inquisitions and the like. Rather than one large monolithic clan, I always wished that the game had presented the Followers as a large group of smaller competing sects, which would work together, but were often as much enemy as ally. In theory you did have this sort of stuff back in the clan's past (especially if you dig into the Typhon-Set concepts) and the concept of different types (warrior/priest/witch). By the end of V20 you finally started to see that with different smaller cults (the Children of Judas, the Church of Black Magdalene, the Hall of Jorgmunder, the House of Eclipse, etc) and I was really digging the direction that the Followers of Set were finally going.. <br /> <br /> Then we get V5 with the Ministry/Followers split, and the concept was initially great because I felt that the Clan had finally gone in the direction I had always wanted to see them go (with the Ministry basically being a gathering for numerous different cults whose primary similarity was in the fact that they rejected Set as the primary god-figure), but it just ended up being kind of a mess as to what the split actual entails, how it actually looks and how you can use that as a major focus for a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T22:30:51-07:00","id":1537747,"title":"","content":"Ehy Charles, as one of the few other OPP forum resident V5 enthusiasts, sorry to hear of your decision.<br /> <br /> I do get most of your points, even though I have less a pessimistic view of authors and their commitment to the IP.<br /> <br /> I miss a more metaplotty approach too: I make a very large use of older source material.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the Gehenna War supplemento, surely It Will follow the same toolbox approach, but we're moving into an interesting subject.<br /> <br /> Cheers and have a blast with all your campaigns, it's what really matters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T02:21:11-07:00","id":1537749,"title":"","content":"Yep, I've plenty of ideas for what happened within the Followers of Set to lead to the &quot;rebrand&quot; (a nice word for a schism, in that clan), but I doubt I'll have a chance to put it to paper. I do appreciate that people can recognise what we were going for in the V5 books we got to make. But - now it's full steam ahead on Curseborne! Which we'll be investing with lore, love, and playability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T11:25:26-07:00","id":1537759,"title":"","content":"I would love to hear what some of your ideas were for the Followers Of Set rebrand Gentleman Gamer as we still view Set as the founder of the clan in our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-21-2024, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T12:34:57-07:00","id":1537872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5#post1537219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know no one will care and it's hardly a thing I should care about but I am leaving V5 behind and returning permanently to V20 with the only exception being incorporating the lore from the Onyx Path publishing books for V5. I've long been a cheerleader for V5 and was a defender of this when they were otherwise very unpopular but I just can't continue onward and I'm not sure I'm even going to buy any more V5 material other than the Visual Novels and Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> It's the handling of Legacy.<br /> <br /> The reason I came back to V:TM was because of the announcement it was going to be the Old World of Darkness revived. I liked what OPP to save the license with V20 but never really jived with the &quot;metaplot agnostic&quot; approach and it was only when they adjusted that I changed my view on things. BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY remained the absolute greatest book ever written for V:TM and celebrated everything I loved about the setting.<br /> <br /> I also came back for CBN and its spin off titles, spending way too much money (money well spent) on the Kickstarter. Same for Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> But the decisions for WoD5 are now exactly the opposite of what I loved.<br /> <br /> Less and less metaplot, less and less NPCs, less and less lore.<br /> <br /> W5 should have been the death blow to my idealism with the hints that W:TA 1-20 were now non-canon and irreconcilable but I stubbornly denied what was in front of my face. I should have known you can only trust people with a genuine love of the material. I don't get that feeling outside of the livestream games.<br /> <br /> So from now on, it'll just be cherishing what OPP has already made and Storyteller's Vault material.<br /> <br /> You guys were right.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lasted longer than me mate, I wish it wasn't so, but here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T12:37:53-07:00","id":1537874,"title":"","content":"It does suck that you lose passion for something that gave you great joy in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T12:00:49-07:00","id":1538051,"title":"","content":"Welcome back to Sanity, friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T13:21:03-07:00","id":1538095,"title":"","content":"I'm glad because you finally acknowledge what some of us have been saying from the beginning, but it's sad because I can guess from how White Wolf has reacted lately, they won't see a fan turned critic and realize they need to change, they will just continue to dig a deeper hole to stick their head in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","user":"Vendrin","date":". 07-06-2024, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T16:26:40-07:00","id":1538101,"title":"","content":"It does seem that way with larger companies, but can VTM really afford that as this game appeals to niche audience like Warhammer 40 K?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T16:52:47-07:00","id":1538103,"title":"","content":"It's worth reminding that VTM is owned by Paradox, who even as a third tierish decently successful videogame studio, have incomes and budgets for which the ttrpg side of their business is more or less a rounding error (remember that they really only bought up most of old white wolf's IPs to make videogames and what all ever off of them, however questionable the success of that specifically has been). They can afford pretty much whatever as far as their investment in tabletop role playing games. This isn't like D&amp;D and Hasbro, which to the rest of the ttrpg industry is mostly some insane, freakish outlier of profits. The tabletop roleplaying aspect of any of this is a borderline vanity project for Paradox for how much the possible success or failure of it could impact them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-04-2024, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T05:27:47-07:00","id":1538120,"title":"","content":"I think Paradox as a company is a bad one. It's only thanks to a few of their games which are these juggernauts on the market that they stay profitable. Aside from those, namely Hearts of Iron IV, Crusader Kings 3 and Stellaris, Paradox as a company would be in a world of trouble. If there's anything that has been a constant in the last few years, it's them fucking up as a publisher.<br /> <br /> Let's go over some of the highlights over the last few years:<ul><li>Lamplighter's Leauge: Paradox had high hopes for the game and Harebrained Games are a good developer (they made those isometric Shadowrun games, for example). But months before the launch, thanks to a lack of support from Paradox 80% of the staff at the studio were let go. Then the game got released to middling reviews (mostly because of the bugs and lack of content) and then Paradox had to announce that it considered <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/paradox-says-the-lamplighters-league-sales-were-a-big-disappointment-confirms-recent-layoffs-at-developer-harebrained-schemes/\" target=\"_blank\">the game a failure</a>. And it doesn't seem like there's any more content planned for it.</li> <li>City Skylines 2: That game launched in a disastrous state. Just google it. A complete failure. The developers are still busy trying to crawl out of that hole and win back the goodwill of the players...</li> <li>Star Trek Infinite: One of the more popular mods for their Sci-Fi-grand strategy game Stellaris revolves around Star Trek. And so Paradox thought: Hey, let's have someone develop an official version. And that's Star Trek Infinite except... the fan-mods are simply better. The game launches, disappoints (middling reviews, lack of interest, sales...) and six months after launch it's announced that <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/paradoxs-grand-strategy-star-trek-infinite-will-receive-no-further-updates\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox will stop any support for the game</a>. In other words, Paradox isn't paying the devs to patch the game or make DLC for it.</li> <li>Life By You: It was pitched as a new Sims-type life-building game. They even created a studio for it called Tectone. Well, a month ago or so, Paradox announced it had decided to <a href=\"https://news.cision.com/paradox-interactive-ab/r/paradox-interactive-cancels-the-release-of-life-by-you-which-impacts-the-second-quarter-with-msek-20,c4002478\" target=\"_blank\">cancel the game</a>. This game had been in development since 2019. Five years of development, a whole studio of developers and 19 million dollars in investment... all flushed down the toilet. Ah, yeah, they closed the studio Tectone as well on top of that.</li> </ul><br /> Bloodlines 2 turning out to be a failure wouldn't be that surprising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T05:55:39-07:00","id":1538122,"title":"","content":"You can dislike Paradox for many frankly correct reasons and point out their various notable failures, that Bloodlines 2 is on track to itself be one more of them, etc. it doesn't change how small the ttrpg industry side of things is to a videogame company of their status. The success or failure or otherwise profitability of Paradox as a company does not depend on how well received VtM 5th the ttrpg is or isn't, in any way, barring such rare times as what we would have to unfortunately call actual media notices such things, and that really only happened once, and it didn't really have anything to do with how well the ttrpg was selling, or how much people liked it, so much as a reference it made to real world politics.<br /> <br /> edit: I feel like people seem to be taking this as some defense of VtM 5th? A game I'm all over these forums for years as disliking pretty hard? It's not. It's just pointing out what reality is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-05-2024, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T06:12:07-07:00","id":1538126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538122#post1538122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dislike Paradox for many frankly correct reasons and point out their various notable failures, that Bloodlines 2 is on track to itself be one more of them, etc. it doesn't change how small the ttrpg industry side of things is to a videogame company of their status. The success or failure of Paradox does not depend on how well received VtM 5th the ttrpg is or isn't, in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. I agree. I just brought up the videogame-side of things because the way they're failing there is an indicator of how and why WOD5E as a ttrpg-property hasn't been utilized to its fullest potential. For whatever reason, Paradox keeps making wrong decisions when it's managing these projects. Sure, they can afford to throw around a lot of money but that doesn't detract from the wasteful quality of their management-decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T02:36:16-07:00","id":1538201,"title":"","content":"V5 is really just a clumsy combination of the worst bits of Masquerade and Requiem, stitched together via some really uninspired and obnoxious writing. It's practically unsalvageable at this point.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, it never really started out strong but there was at least some potential there (see <i>Chicago Folios, Fall of London</i>) but it got awfully bad once the dreadful Sabbat supplement came out and has been getting worse ever since with no signs of improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T20:45:54-07:00","id":1538222,"title":"","content":"Yes I didn't care for the Sabbat sourcebook in general and I had hoped that there would be more lore sheets for the Lasombra and Tziscme clans and there wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T01:13:56-07:00","id":1538227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537292#post1537292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a very narrow, very tiny game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of 5th either but this reminded me of what I've come to think about the line in general. V5, to me, feels like someone's heavily houseruled version of the game, it's narrowed down to just one point of view, one style of play, one single campaign, and the ST is very stricxt about not allowing anything other than their specifc vision of vampire 'life'.<br /> <br /> Then Paradox came along and asked that ST to publish their version as V5.<br /> <br /> I will point out that I'm biased towards metaplot agnosticism but that's because I like to make up my own stories for my set of players. I only use the lore to support those stories and where possible bend the story to fit the lore, but if the choice is between lore or a good story then story comes first. Which I feel is kind of opposite to the way the 'secret ST' behind V5 operates.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T03:52:06-07:00","id":1538229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538227#post1538227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will point out that I'm biased towards metaplot agnosticism but that's because I like to make up my own stories for my set of players. I only use the lore to support those stories and where possible bend the story to fit the lore, but if the choice is between lore or a good story then story comes first. Which I feel is kind of opposite to the way the 'secret ST' behind V5 operates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think lore is meant to feed the imagination and story. The attempt to make the lore irrelevant and &quot;generic up&quot; the vampires of the setting as much as they have is what killed the setting.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine said this is basically what happened to D&amp;D. TSR wasn't afraid to make D&amp;D settings WEIRD but when they were reduced to one setting, things became more and more generic until it stopped having any real flavor.<br /> <br /> 5th Edition does not have the 13 Clans, not really. Not the Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Inconnu, or Black Hand.<br /> <br /> It has Hunters, Snooty Vampires, Street Vampires, and Mean Stupid Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T09:38:41-07:00","id":1538238,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Ahh, I\u2019m sad to hear it. I\u2019ve always been more of a lurker here only posting once every few months, but I always enjoyed your enthusiasm contrasting with the omnipresent dislike of v5 over here.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">It\u2019s been a while since I ran v5, since I\u2019ve been busy building my own RPG system and I have way too many unread v5 book, but it does seem like the good parts of WOD 5 are behind us.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">To me v5 felt like a great pitch meeting. I felt like it had a bunch of interesting new ideas that could have been developed and refined.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I loved the initial v5 lore and the mysteries they introduced.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I fell in love with the hunger dice system which I thought was a stroke of genius. It suddenly incorporated vampiric hunger as a mechanic you could feel and visualize instead of relying on some magic points with a very controllable limit.</span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">However, some subpart of the system I didn\u2019t quite like, I preferred damage and hit points in Requiem 2<sup>nd</sup>. I originally liked the discipline powers of v5, but after a while I felt like they were closer to magical spells, or MMO abilities than discipline.</span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">In the end I ended up creating my own mix of Requiem and v5 using the parts I loved from both.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I guess i\u2019ll stay tuned and keep updated on how it all evolves in the future.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T18:23:18-07:00","id":1538264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1537742#post1537742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, why NOT just say, &quot;The Kuei Jin are non-canon now and we're never going to address them.&quot; It would have saved some trouble, I think and I generally approve of that decision.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>well in contrast there's also <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/435620/Kindred-of-the-East-The-Relentless-Age\" target=\"_blank\">KIndred of the east restless age </a>does actually address the many problematic aspects of it's source material and from what little dissection I've seen, it seems to have succeeded on that front. The games author Hsienfan is writing a sort of follow up that centered around the <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/changeling-the-dreaming-in-the-realm-of-gods-and-dreams-live-drafting-a-hsien-reboot.911145/\" target=\"_blank\">Hsien </a>(called little gods in the drafts).<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not even getting into <a href=\"https://songoftrillium.tumblr.com/werewolfessentials\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf the: Essentials</a> Which essentially (pardon the pun) has the goals of doing what Restless age has done with WtA and more since the main author of the project is planning on writing five whole books for it. Basically making the project a whole new edition of WtA.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T20:18:59-07:00","id":1538279,"title":"","content":"It's funny, because this is one place where it would have been better for White Wolf if they had done like W5, and said that V5 was more of a spiritual successor to VtM than a direct new edition, and that many parts of the older editions would still be canon, but some stuff (like KotE) no longer would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T20:35:03-07:00","id":1538280,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Kindred of the East wasn't to well received by many of the posters here. I take that it had lots of bad stereotypes and stuff that didn't appeal to anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T22:48:15-07:00","id":1538287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538280#post1538280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Kindred of the East wasn't to well received by many of the posters here. I take that it had lots of <b>bad stereotypes and stuff</b> that didn't appeal to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that and the core book outright said that Asians have different souls to the point where western vampires can't actually embrace them. Or at least something similar. Which is yeah... You can see the unfortunate implications...<br /> <br /> Restless age dose away with all that and make it clear the Kuei Jin are distinctly different creatures from the kindred that happens to fill the same niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T04:47:46-07:00","id":1538290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538280#post1538280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Kindred of the East wasn't to well received by many of the posters here. I take that it had lots of bad stereotypes and stuff that didn't appeal to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been a big fan of the concept, there's some issues with particular word choices\u200b and a few ideas that haven't aged very well, but I love the transhumanism and inhuman enlightenment. I also really like the concept of the Yama Kings and how they make White Wolf's Asian setting more crossover friendly, giving a big bad guy that you can use to more easily run mixed Chronicles. Really, Kindred of the East was my favorite White Wolf game, but it was a product of the 90's and the early 2000's, and I can I see why White Wolf wouldn't want to go back to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538287#post1538287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that and the core book outright said that Asians have different souls to the point where western vampires can't actually embrace them. Or at least something similar. Which is yeah... You can see the unfortunate implications...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you got that idea, but it's not true at all. There have always been lots of Asian Kindred, even whole Bloodlines like the Anda. What's different about Asia is that the Yama Kings (powerful spirits) betrayed the Jade Emperor (basically God) tore up huge sections of the Umbra and the Underworld and created kingdoms and then began stealing and torturing the souls of the dead to get power. Sometimes souls can escape from the 1000 Hells and when they do, they emerge as Eastern Kindred. The Jade Emperor created this process so that some sinners can have a second chance at redemption, and the Yama Kings have to deal with their soul-theft coming back to bite them in the ass by creating their most dedicated enemies. <br /> <br /> The Eastern Kindred do have a Higher (Hun) and Lower Soul (Po), but so does every human - in VtM the Kindred's lower soul is more active than in normal humans and is the Beast. In Wraith: the Oblivion it gains intelligence and becomes the Shadow. Eastern Kindred's Po operates more like the Shadow and is sentient, but ultimately their soul isn't much different than normal, other than the fact that they went to Hell and crawled back out. <br /> <br /> Ultimately though it's a game mechanic. Like with Mummy - they have 7 parts to their soul. But it's not like the game is saying Egyptians have unique souls from everyone else in the world and can't be Embraced or anything like that. Just that the magical system that was used to create Mummies split their soul into 7 different parts, it's not supposed to be saying anything about actual living people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T04:53:21-07:00","id":1538291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538280#post1538280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Kindred of the East wasn't to well received by many of the posters here. I take that it had lots of bad stereotypes and stuff that didn't appeal to anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I bought the book many years ago for the collection sake, but I admit never gave it a whole thorough read.<br /> <br /> Aside from taking into account that it's not my language and at the time I still struggled with english a bit<br /> <br /> I think the main problem was that it felt like an unnecessary complication of the game world and a whole bunch of rules and systems and mythology to learn from zero, for something that it was sold in the title as &quot;Kindred of the East&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't think that something like the Kuei Jin was strictly a bad idea, since VtM is based on modern reinterpretation of folklore creatures that by know have little in common with their myth and legends inspiration.<br /> So the same could have been done with the 'hopping vampires' as well.<br /> <br /> They could exist in the world of darkness, but alongside the more known to players kindred instead of &quot;in Asia you don't have the usual Kindred at all, you have this instead&quot;.<br /> <br /> Something called Kindred of the East should have been a sourcebook like Veil of Night, something that tells you how the usual clans are called and what they're up to in Asia, maybe alongside a few new clans or bloodlines like the Gaki.<br /> And then, in an appendix of the book you could have had a character option for the Kuei Jin<br /> <br /> Or you could have a smaller book like World of Darkness Mummy, which presents you what effectly is a player option in a Vampire chronicle.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that trying to come up with a reinterpratation of the jiangshi for the World of Darkness wasn't a bad idea, and they came up with some neat stuff.<br /> But they overcommitted to it<br /> <br /> But overcommitting to niche ideas was the most White Wolf thing probably.<br /> <br /> I've recently discovered that Changeling had 45 published books.<br /> As much as I love the game and its ambitions, what niche RPG can afford 45 supplements in the span of ten years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T05:47:55-07:00","id":1538295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538291#post1538291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main problem was that it felt like an unnecessary complication of the game world and a whole bunch of rules and systems and mythology to learn from zero, for something that it was sold in the title as &quot;Kindred of the East&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one of the goals of Relentless age is try to simplify all the all the stuff in the source material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T06:44:39-07:00","id":1538298,"title":"","content":"Basically, the problem of Kindred of the East is the orientalism was pretty bad.<br /> <br /> But ALSO, the &quot;Planescape&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> The short version being that TSR tried to make a bunch of lines to bring new fans into Dungeons and Dragons in the Nineties, which White Wolf followed suit regarding, but all it did was divide the fanbase. Introducing Kindred of the East didn't add any new Vampire: The Masquerade fans, it just divided the vampire fanbase further.<br /> <br /> It didn't help the Kuei Jin were trying to be more respectful by giving local vampire legends of Asia their own origin separate from Caine but, well, that didn't actually help because there's no &quot;Asian&quot; vampire.<br /> <br /> Kuei Jin being the vampires of Japan, India, China, and Korea is JUST as orientalist as making the Cainites the source of their local vampires because they have just as much in common culture wise.<br /> <br /> Japan is fine with Western vampires but don't pretend that the Kuei Jin are &quot;their&quot; vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-09-2024, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T11:55:09-07:00","id":1538307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538298#post1538298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the problem of Kindred of the East is the orientalism was pretty bad.<br /> <br /> But ALSO, the &quot;Planescape&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> The short version being that TSR tried to make a bunch of lines to bring new fans into Dungeons and Dragons in the Nineties, which White Wolf followed suit regarding, but all it did was divide the fanbase. Introducing Kindred of the East didn't add any new Vampire: The Masquerade fans, it just divided the vampire fanbase further.<br /> <br /> It didn't help the Kuei Jin were trying to be more respectful by giving local vampire legends of Asia their own origin separate from Caine but, well, that didn't actually help because there's no &quot;Asian&quot; vampire.<br /> <br /> Kuei Jin being the vampires of Japan, India, China, and Korea is JUST as orientalist as making the Cainites the source of their local vampires because they have just as much in common culture wise.<br /> <br /> Japan is fine with Western vampires but don't pretend that the Kuei Jin are &quot;their&quot; vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a tricky one the Kuei Jin are a mix of the jianhsgi and several other asian sources to make something similar to the Western pop culture vampire because as you said, their is no asian equivalent, for the time they're actually a pretty good crack at it they just now look dates. Making everyone western vampires itself is ultimately worse since it's saying whitey monsters rule everywhere ( a point w5 completely missed incidentally). The solution would be to refine and update the Kuei Jin (such as making it dharmist hell rather than asian hell) while establishing a kindred presence in asia for people who want to do that. This could even be a useful reflection of the cosmopolitan nature of the world were both groups are having to deal with enclaves of their natural rivals.<br /> Of course theirs no way Paradox would go for this and the fandom is fundamentally unpleasable on this issue. so it'll never happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:11:07-07:00","id":1538309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538307#post1538307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a tricky one the Kuei Jin are a mix of the jianhsgi and several other asian sources to make something similar to the Western pop culture vampire because as you said, their is no asian equivalent, for the time they're actually a pretty good crack at it they just now look dates. Making everyone western vampires itself is ultimately worse since it's saying whitey monsters rule everywhere ( a point w5 completely missed incidentally). The solution would be to refine and update the Kuei Jin (such as making it dharmist hell rather than asian hell) while establishing a kindred presence in asia for people who want to do that. This could even be a useful reflection of the cosmopolitan nature of the world were both groups are having to deal with enclaves of their natural rivals.<br /> Of course theirs no way Paradox would go for this and the fandom is fundamentally unpleasable on this issue. so it'll never happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it, though? Because saying that the vampire are from the Middle East and the same race but culturally the country they were Embraced in doesn't seem like a big colonialist statement.<br /> <br /> Mind you, part of this may be the fact they canonized Caine as the origin.<br /> <br /> But the fact is that if they're not Cainites and have different rules.<br /> <br /> It's not Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> And people who buy the game in, say, Tokyo or Hong Kong, want to play Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hellsing, for example, still uses Dracula instead of local demons despite being a Japanese take on vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:25:20-07:00","id":1538312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538309#post1538309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it, though? Because saying that the vampire are from the Middle East and the same race but culturally the country they were Embraced in doesn't seem like a big colonialist statement.<br /> <br /> Mind you, part of this may be the fact they canonized Caine as the origin.<br /> <br /> But the fact is that if they're not Cainites and have different rules.<br /> <br /> It's not Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> And people who buy the game in, say, Tokyo or Hong Kong, want to play Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hellsing, for example, still uses Dracula instead of local demons despite being a Japanese take on vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IRL Vtm vampires are western pop culture vampire it'd be like all wraith the oblivion being all about onryo. They're only really from the middle east in a biblical lore sense aka in the same sense the Catholic church is from the middle east. True which is were you could have western enclaves of kindred in asia and Kuei Jin.<br /> <br /> Helsing probably isnt a great example of this as the show is set in the United kingdom which ironically makes it closer to kindred of the east in that it's a Japanese interpretation of western pop culture/folklore.<br /> Tokyo ghoul is probably closer to what you're going for as it's a eastern interpretation of western idea's of undead in asia (with some superficial links to ghuls)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T13:09:14-07:00","id":1538314,"title":"","content":"Also, even in Hellsing, there was room for vampires without V:tM-style sires. So maybe V5 should have just mixed Kindred up with Hungry Dead to really shake everyone up, as vampires rise from the grave independently of any other (like KotE) and go on to turn others into vampires (V:tM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:08:00-07:00","id":1538323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538307#post1538307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The solution would be to refine and update the Kuei Jin (such as making it dharmist hell rather than asian hell)</b> while establishing a kindred presence in asia for people who want to do that. This could even be a useful reflection of the cosmopolitan nature of the world were both groups are having to deal with enclaves of their natural rivals.<br /> Of course theirs no way Paradox would go for this and the fandom is fundamentally unpleasable on this issue. so it'll never happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded part is literally what <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/435620/Kindred-of-the-East-The-Relentless-Age\" target=\"_blank\">the relentless age </a>did and pretty Universally prased as far as niche fan games go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:10:58-07:00","id":1538324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538309#post1538309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it, though? Because saying that the vampire are from the Middle East and the same race but culturally the country they were Embraced in doesn't seem like a big colonialist statement.<br /> <br /> Mind you, part of this may be the fact they canonized Caine as the origin.<br /> <br /> But the fact is that if they're not Cainites and have different rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the idea of a western-inspired vampire isn't terribly problematic, the issue is with VtM having its roots in the Bible and and the setting generally going, &quot;Yup, the Bible is correct and other religions/cultures are wrong.&quot; You have a handful of other alternative origin like the Followers of Set, but the rest of the gameline makes it pretty clear that Set is full of bullshit and he's not really the first vampire or anything like that. it's pretty clear that those guys are wrong. And you have say, the African vampires, but it's also painfully obvious that their origin story is also wrong and they're descendants of the Biblical vampires due to the way their Generation limits work.<br /> <br /> I wish VtM was more culturally agnostic and presented a lot of different possibilities for Vampiric origins. The idea that Book of Genesis is essentially a historical document is cool for the type of game VtM is supposed to be, but it's also problematic because of what that says about the history of other cultures. Since, by the time KotE was written, you couldn't really divorce Kindred from the Biblical origins (despite a few half-hearted attempts to do so), I think trying to create another type of origin story for a different part of the world (the 10,000 Immortals) was a cool idea. It didn't work out in practice, but I really respect the attempt and think we got the chassis for a really cool game, and IMO, the best overall setting for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:32:40-07:00","id":1538325,"title":"","content":"One thing you have to like about VTR is that they didn't have a concrete origin for the undead and you could come up with your own ideas. As I mentioned before I'm quite taken with the idea of Set being the first vampire and not Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:46:19-07:00","id":1538327,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the problem with Orientalism, or any other racist otherism, is to write about a place and culture without input from the people.<br /> <br /> KotE is the &quot;best bad idea&quot; in WoD, a lot of people like it, and it certainly could have worked with minor adjustments.<br /> <br /> But it was a part of the process of making Asia work entirely different from the rest of the setting just for the sake of being &quot;more Asian&quot; <b>for American readers</b>, all the while ignoring what actual Asian players wanted for their countries in the setting. And in the process making the new &quot;Asian&quot; options the only one canonical for most of the place.<br /> <br /> Making KotE a rarer splat and letting most of Asia be &quot;normal&quot; Vampires would probably solve most problems. The &quot;Bible is True&quot; problem is also a thing, but a broader problem than just Orientalism. But again: have consultants that can bring input from actual Asians for a change is the actual key to solve the conundrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T16:19:23-07:00","id":1538330,"title":"","content":"For people who are interested in KotE or feel like they might be if it had been handled differently, you might like this alternate draft of the setting/game that a writer on the RPG.Net forums did. I was not a fan of KotE but I found this to be very interesting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.893999/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T18:29:10-07:00","id":1538335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538330#post1538330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For people who are interested in KotE or feel like they might be if it had been handled differently, you might like this alternate draft of the setting/game that a writer on the RPG.Net forums did. I was not a fan of KotE but I found this to be very interesting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...reboot.893999/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>To add the STV link: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/435620\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/435620</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T00:13:14-07:00","id":1538346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538327#post1538327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making KotE a rarer splat and letting most of Asia be &quot;normal&quot; Vampires would probably solve most problems. The &quot;Bible is True&quot; problem is also a thing, but a broader problem than just Orientalism. But again: have consultants that can bring input from actual Asians for a change is the actual key to solve the conundrum.</div> </div> </div> </div> Imo that'd actually be worse since itd be western (specifically) american pop culture undead everywere on earth with some local flavour <br /> my suggestion would be to rather than have a asian consultants for vtm would be to commision an asian rpg company to do a write up for koe with a mandate of &quot;less problematic, keep whats appropriate change what doesnt&quot; and have some cultural consultants from other nations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T03:54:15-07:00","id":1538351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538346#post1538346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo that'd actually be worse since itd be western (specifically) american pop culture undead everywere on earth with some local flavour<br /> my suggestion would be to rather than have a asian consultants for vtm would be to commision an asian rpg company to do a write up for koe with a mandate of &quot;less problematic, keep whats appropriate change what doesnt&quot; and have some cultural consultants from other nations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, that's flat out not what Asian PLAYERS wanted though. They did NOT want to play Jiangshi when they played Vampire: The Masquerade. This is just pointing to facts but all of the Hong Kong, Japanese, and Korean WOD gamers have always wanted to play the Thirteen Clans.<br /> <br /> Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The stats are pretty clear the Western vampires are the ones that local fan groups want to play and it applies to Asian Americans as well.<br /> <br /> Part of this is that the Kuei Jin will NEVER be anything more than an attempt to push away Asian players from the actual game they want to play, however well intentioned. 90% of the material in the game is for Western vampires and they're probably wanting to play the game because they're familiar with Western media or local versions of Western vampires ala Hellsing or Vampire: Hunter D.<br /> <br /> <b>Plus there's one other small issue</b><br /> <br /> There's also the more esoteric element of this. Which is jiangshi and other Kuei Jin-esque monsters...aren't remotely like Western vampires. Which Asian players know and wonder WTF people are talking about when WOD players to get people to play them.<br /> <br /> When they see V:TM and think vampires, they're thinking of the sexy beautiful Western vampires and their stories of competing politics because Jiangshi are....not sexy vampires. Which is a kind of blindingly obvious flaw with this argument to begin with. You can't stuff local mythology into the role that was developed organically in another. It represents a fundamental misunderstanding of the subject matter.<br /> <br /> Sort of like if you're, say Greek, and someone tried to do a book about minotaurs and insisting that there's this cult of sexy Greek minotaurs with awesome powers and they have a society of minotaurs competing. Then telling you, as a Greek person, you have to play a minotaur because it is your culture versus a vampire BUT minotaurs are just the same as Western vampires.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're insane because it is. Minotaur: The Eternal Struggle is not the game they want or care to play.<br /> <br /> Which may be why Kuei Jin can never be &quot;fixed&quot; for the majority of people. It's not that it can't be well written but its trying to tell people what they can't or can't like on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-10-2024, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T06:06:42-07:00","id":1538355,"title":"","content":"We should bear in mind that not all of us have Phipps experiences with Asian and other minority players and that, for instance, My Indonesian, Malaysian, Singaporean, Polynesian and Melanesian players all were quite pleased with our less Sino-centric Hungry Dead Chronicles over the years and had little interest in the US focused mostly visual media based vampires experience given by VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:11:18-07:00","id":1538365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538351#post1538351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, that's flat out not what Asian PLAYERS wanted though. They did NOT want to play Jiangshi when they played Vampire: The Masquerade. This is just pointing to facts but all of the Hong Kong, Japanese, and Korean WOD gamers have always wanted to play the Thirteen Clans.<br /> <br /> Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The stats are pretty clear the Western vampires are the ones that local fan groups want to play and it applies to Asian Americans as well.<br /> <br /> Part of this is that the Kuei Jin will NEVER be anything more than an attempt to push away Asian players from the actual game they want to play, however well intentioned. 90% of the material in the game is for Western vampires and they're probably wanting to play the game because they're familiar with Western media or local versions of Western vampires ala Hellsing or Vampire: Hunter D.<br /> <br /> <b>Plus there's one other small issue</b><br /> <br /> There's also the more esoteric element of this. Which is jiangshi and other Kuei Jin-esque monsters...aren't remotely like Western vampires. Which Asian players know and wonder WTF people are talking about when WOD players to get people to play them.<br /> <br /> When they see V:TM and think vampires, they're thinking of the sexy beautiful Western vampires and their stories of competing politics because Jiangshi are....not sexy vampires. Which is a kind of blindingly obvious flaw with this argument to begin with. You can't stuff local mythology into the role that was developed organically in another. It represents a fundamental misunderstanding of the subject matter.<br /> <br /> Sort of like if you're, say Greek, and someone tried to do a book about minotaurs and insisting that there's this cult of sexy Greek minotaurs with awesome powers and they have a society of minotaurs competing. Then telling you, as a Greek person, you have to play a minotaur because it is your culture versus a vampire BUT minotaurs are just the same as Western vampires.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're insane because it is. <b>Minotaur: The Eternal Struggle</b> is not the game they want or care to play.<br /> <br /> Which may be why Kuei Jin can never be &quot;fixed&quot; for the majority of people. It's not that it can't be well written but its trying to tell people what they can't or can't like on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grontar: the Frutang?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:27:38-07:00","id":1538368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538351#post1538351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhh, that's flat out not what Asian PLAYERS wanted though. They did NOT want to play Jiangshi when they played Vampire: The Masquerade. This is just pointing to facts but all of the Hong Kong, Japanese, and Korean WOD gamers have always wanted to play the Thirteen Clans.<br /> <br /> Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The stats are pretty clear the Western vampires are the ones that local fan groups want to play and it applies to Asian Americans as well.<br /> <br /> Part of this is that the Kuei Jin will NEVER be anything more than an attempt to push away Asian players from the actual game they want to play, however well intentioned. 90% of the material in the game is for Western vampires and they're probably wanting to play the game because they're familiar with Western media or local versions of Western vampires ala Hellsing or Vampire: Hunter D.<br /> <br /> <b>Plus there's one other small issue</b><br /> <br /> There's also the more esoteric element of this. Which is jiangshi and other Kuei Jin-esque monsters...aren't remotely like Western vampires. Which Asian players know and wonder WTF people are talking about when WOD players to get people to play them.<br /> <br /> When they see V:TM and think vampires, they're thinking of the sexy beautiful Western vampires and their stories of competing politics because Jiangshi are....not sexy vampires. Which is a kind of blindingly obvious flaw with this argument to begin with. You can't stuff local mythology into the role that was developed organically in another. It represents a fundamental misunderstanding of the subject matter.<br /> <br /> Sort of like if you're, say Greek, and someone tried to do a book about minotaurs and insisting that there's this cult of sexy Greek minotaurs with awesome powers and they have a society of minotaurs competing. Then telling you, as a Greek person, you have to play a minotaur because it is your culture versus a vampire BUT minotaurs are just the same as Western vampires.<br /> <br /> It sounds like you're insane because it is. Minotaur: The Eternal Struggle is not the game they want or care to play.<br /> <br /> Which may be why Kuei Jin can never be &quot;fixed&quot; for the majority of people. It's not that it can't be well written but its trying to tell people what they can't or can't like on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good comment so requires a lot to unpack.<br /> <br /> Firstly i'd be reluctant to comment on universality to any group. I know I can't really guarantee my own voice as a Celt for the fianna. I think we can however say their was a general antipathy present for koe with Asian sections of the community in your experience. This is fair enough, I would however state it is a gross overstatement to say koe was a deliberate attempt to box Asian players away from other players, more likely the authors saw a way to expand the setting and make money. I doubt anyone in old white wolf objected to people from hong kong running vtm anymore than they'd object to them buying and running werewolf wild west.<br /> <br /> I also find it hard to buy that asian players don't understand why a pop culture interpretation of Asian undead wouldn't appeal to people when they themselves are by your argument, very invested in a pop culture interpretation of western undead. VTM vampire are not in any sense of the word folklore vampires, they're nothing like folklore vampires.They're influences at best go back to gothic horror literature. With that precedence it's perfectly viable to construct a equivalent and koe gave it a solid crack for the period.<br /> <br /> You probably could run a game purely off one specific Greek monster, the trope isnt developed enough as it is but you can very easily develop that idea into something more robust....that was more or less the intent of beast: the primordial (Yes I know, but it could have been done well) or to a lesser degree changeling the lost.<br /> <br /> I really don't think the fuckability of a pc is as vital a requisite as you presume, especially considering at least two of the clans look like shit.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it's telling people anymore than I'm telling them to play werewolf since vampire is more popular, what I'm saying is it's an interesting concept which has a lot of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-10-2024, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:31:15-07:00","id":1538369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538355#post1538355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should bear in mind that not all of us have Phipps experiences with Asian and other minority players and that, for instance, My Indonesian, Malaysian, Singaporean, Polynesian and Melanesian players all were quite pleased with our less Sino-centric Hungry Dead Chronicles over the years and had little interest in the US focused mostly visual media based vampires experience given by VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience of asian players is that they'v mostly been into CoC and d&amp;d I've only met one asian wod player and she was really into playing Hermetics.<br /> <br /> EDIT-was Koe even translated into any asian languages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T09:52:51-07:00","id":1538370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538355#post1538355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should bear in mind that not all of us have Phipps experiences with Asian and other minority players and that, for instance, My Indonesian, Malaysian, Singaporean, Polynesian and Melanesian players all were quite pleased with our less Sino-centric Hungry Dead Chronicles over the years and had little interest in the US focused mostly visual media based vampires experience given by VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct and I am only speaking from a lot of personal anecdotes.<br /> <br /> I don't hate the Kuei-Jin. I just think it needed:<br /> <br /> A. More Asian writers<br /> <br /> B. Shouldn't have been a Vampire Supplement.<br /> <br /> C. We needed a whole book on Asian versions of the 13 with their own entirely plausible origin for the Antediluvians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T12:03:22-07:00","id":1538383,"title":"","content":"They could have done a more spirit based game. Something like &quot;Rabits, Dragons, Monkeys&quot; China/Japan/India style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T13:05:15-07:00","id":1538384,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if they would have done a good treatment of that Crytash2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T13:32:11-07:00","id":1538385,"title":"","content":"At least it would have been more unique than just creating another VTM_Just Different\u2122 clone. I am sure there are cool ideas out there from East Asian writers that could be developed in that direction. What makes VTM strong is partially the cultural baggage; otherwise, VTR would have been much more successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T19:10:11-07:00","id":1538402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538346#post1538346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Imo that'd actually be worse since itd be western QUOTE=Ragged Robin;n1538346]<br /> Imo that'd actually be worse since itd be western (specifically) american pop culture undead everywere on earth with some local flavour<br /> my suggestion would be to rather than have a asian consultants for vtm would be to commision an asian rpg company to do a write up for koe with a mandate of &quot;less problematic, keep whats appropriate change what doesnt&quot; and have some cultural consultants from other nations.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is that it ignores the people who wanted to play VtM with canon material. Part of the problem is precisely to decide which splats they should play without their input.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I think both consultants and local writers are much needed. By the way, it is how C20 came to be.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that they're already, well, Asian. They don't come to VtM looking for Asian legends, they have their own local publishers making this without much of a thought. Again: the main point is to let them say what they want, what they like and what they feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538351#post1538351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which may be why Kuei Jin can never be &quot;fixed&quot; for the majority of people. It's not that it can't be well written but its trying to tell people what they can't or can't like on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only here I have to disagree.<br /> <br /> KotE can't be fixed as long as the whole purpose is to make the &quot;correct vampire for Asia&quot;. But as long as we drop such a purpose, it can exist as its own thing, as another addition to the WoD.<br /> <br /> I don't think in any way that the splat is a bad thing to have around, we only need to drop the idea that they dominate the area in such a way as to drive the major Sects out of most of the continent.<br /> <br /> Specially because erasure is a thing. Simply ignoring KotE isn't a fix, it may cause more harm than good. Asking how they feel about ditching the whole splat is a very different question from what they thought of the splat in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T10:19:03-07:00","id":1538905,"title":"","content":"If I can say, as someone who had very little love for V5, which has since waned further, and almost no love for W5 at any point. Thank you to CTPhipps and others for working to curb the negativity on this forum. There are plenty of other places on the Net for folks to be vitriolic at each other over matters of taste, and I myself am guilty of trying to bring that here on occasion, if out of habit for no other reason; and I am grateful to people here who wanted to maintain this as a place for (relatively) respectful discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T14:14:04-07:00","id":1538918,"title":"","content":"Yes this message board is quite good at keeping things civil here and keeping flame wars to minimum unlike other sites I had to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T23:44:14-07:00","id":1538962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538370#post1538370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct and I am only speaking from a lot of personal anecdotes.<br /> <br /> I don't hate the Kuei-Jin. I just think it needed:<br /> <br /> A. More Asian writers<br /> <br /> B. Shouldn't have been a Vampire Supplement.<br /> <br /> C. We needed a whole book on Asian versions of the 13 with their own entirely plausible origin for the Antediluvians.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lost me when you mentioned the 13, the entire point of bothering to do something like this would be.they are separate entities from cainites, not 'western' (I know a lot of western myths are from the fertile crescent and Eurasian steppe, but blame the way we name culture groups) myths colonising the rest of the world again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T01:08:55-07:00","id":1538964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538402#post1538402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that it ignores the people who wanted to play VtM with canon material. Part of the problem is precisely to decide which splats they should play without their input.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I think both consultants and local writers are much needed. By the way, it is how C20 came to be.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that they're already, well, Asian. They don't come to VtM looking for Asian legends, they have their own local publishers making this without much of a thought. Again: the main point is to let them say what they want, what they like and what they feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont really consider it a binary anymore than the presence of lupines excludes countryside chronicles. Maybe kaifeng doesnt have any kindred but hong kong almost certainly does. Likewise i dont object to the kue jinn controlling los angeles. To say nothing of ignoring canon which is typically the norm in my experiance anyway.<br /> <br /> oddly it reminds me of objection of specific sects controlling specific cities. Its a slightly odd issue which cannot really be resolved due to the nature of the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-21-2024, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:14:56-07:00","id":1538972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538962#post1538962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You lost me when you mentioned the 13, the entire point of bothering to do something like this would be.they are separate entities from cainites, not 'western' (I know a lot of western myths are from the fertile crescent and Eurasian steppe, but blame the way we name culture groups) myths colonising the rest of the world again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't understand 3.<br /> <br /> 3 isn't saying the Kuei Jin would be Cainites. If they did a Kuei Jin supplement, it would be a wholly separate line like Changeling.<br /> <br /> No, there would be supplements for Vampire: The Masquerade for Asia though because they would be wholly separate lines as they have nothing in common anymore than vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> It would allow people in Asia to play V:TM as well as this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:17:17-07:00","id":1538974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538964#post1538964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I dont really consider it a binary anymore than the presence of lupines excludes countryside chronicles. Maybe kaifeng doesnt have any kindred but hong kong almost certainly does. Likewise i dont object to the kue jinn controlling los angeles. To say nothing of ignoring canon which is typically the norm in my experiance anyway.<br /> <br /> oddly it reminds me of objection of specific sects controlling specific cities. Its a slightly odd issue which cannot really be resolved due to the nature of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the solution there is to change canon but other than giving up an a setting having any lore whatsoever, there's no solution.<br /> <br /> Saying, &quot;I hate the Camarilla controlling Chicago&quot; is the same as, &quot;I hate Waterdeep not being a city of Drow.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T11:21:03-07:00","id":1538977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538974#post1538974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the solution there is to change canon but other than giving up an a setting having any lore whatsoever, there's no solution.<br /> <br /> Saying, &quot;I hate the Camarilla controlling Chicago&quot; is the same as, &quot;I hate Waterdeep not being a city of Drow.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much yeah. I always frowned at europe being the camarilla static doom fort in game but it makes semse from a meta plot sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T15:29:25-07:00","id":1538995,"title":"","content":"There are many, many mentions of Cainite populations and activities in Asia throughout the lifespan of VtM but they are scattered through a hundred different books....some not even VtM books...so collecting the references together into a single volume would be a useful STV project to put the ' no Kindred in Asia' furphy to rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T20:07:09-07:00","id":1539002,"title":"","content":"I think I generally agree with those who have said that to fix the KotE issue, you would just have to rewrite whole elements of the lore and setting. If one chooses to do so, there are many ways to do it, which can appeal to different people.<br /> I myself would probably go for a specific notion of vampire, of the VtM kind but maybe with some mechanic closer to Orun and Aye or the Dharmas and P'o rather than Humanity and the Paths of Enlightenment (simply because I like the first ones mechanically and narratively more than the VtM system) or closer to VtR 2e's Humanity system. This kind of vampire is everywhere in the world. Local folklore &quot;vampires&quot; are either local variations through clan, bloodline and custom discipline powers, or a different supernatural creature altogether typical of that area. The 13 clans (with some apocryphal clan here and there credited to more obscure possible Antediluvians) are not centered in the West, but spread all over, even if the game lore is mainly written by paying attention to the Western history of vampires (for now, just because that's how the metaplot has been written so far). The European Ventrue, for example, have no more relevance than the Indian or African or Korean ones. By calling in consultants from different regions, more lore can be developed to give vampires of other parts of the world their own detailed history. KotE and KotEK disappear and their material (along with the Drowned Legacies) is reabsorbed into the 13 clans without disagreeable (to use a soft term) ideas like that that African vampires are essentially Cainite but so oblivious to their own history that they can't tell and think they're a different species. I find that idea quite insulting.<br /> I could go on, but I think I would end up either end up describing something very close to VtR 2e but with a fixed metaplot, or doubling down on the criticism on how VtM and its supplements (including VDA) have from the beginning been West-centric, thought attempts have been made to fix that with each edition. But ultimately there are issues in the metaplot and foundations. One only needs to think of the imbalance between the European clans, which can in fact be anywhere in Cainite history, the Middle Eastern clans (Setites and Assamites), which are an odd idea in the first place, the near absence of proper Indian clans (aside from the Ravnos to an extent) despite the many bloodlines there, and then the total absence of clans from elsewhere because KotE handled the &quot;East&quot; (silly notion given how much Asian cultures - including Middle Eastern - are historically bound together), KotEK implied their clans were just bloodlines of the 13, and the Drowned Legacies are not even well defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T02:08:49-07:00","id":1539005,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Kote The Relentless Age makes it clear that being the follower of the Dharmas isn't tired to ones race and it only takes a welling hungry dead to teach a respective student as this excerpt has shown:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you play as a non-Asian Hungry Dead?<br /> <br /> The answer is yes. People all over the world go to hell and return, and none of the Dharmas are closed off on account of one's racial or ethnic background.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that, given a long enough time span, concepts like &quot;racism&quot; and &quot;resentment over colonialism&quot; aren't so cut and dry-- Vietnam, for example, struggled with Chinese imperialism for centuries longer than they ever struggled against the French and Americans. Even if the young have legitimate reasons to hold on to grudges, the older Hungry Dead who teach the Dharmas often don't think in such terms; they've seen too much come and go. Refusing to teach a new Hungry Dead the glorious way of the Resplendent Crane, simply because he's a white Canadian named Smith? That feels like a dereliction of one's heavenly duties, not a righteous stance.<br /> <br /> With that said, there are certain things to keep in mind if you want to play a non-Asian Hungry Dead:<br /> <br /> 1) Your game is probably set in urban California. With some isolated and rare exceptions which will be discussed later, the Hungry Dead don't have a society or culture native to Europe or the Americas. The world west of India is a Cainite world, and the Hungry Dead who rise within it have a very strong incentive to see themselves as Caitiff or as tragically abandoned Sabbat shovelheads. Only places where the Dharmas have made inroads, like California (and to a much lesser extent in London and New York, under the heavy shadow of the Camarilla), are where the Hungry Dead have a greater chance to be found and taught what they really are.<br /> <br /> 2) Your character is very likely to have ties to an East Asian, Southeast Asian, or South Asian culture. While a wandering Ravnos can teach your character the Pure Illusion-Truth, or your character could get tangled up with a Celestial Tribe cult or some Scorpion Eaters hiding out in Mexicali, it's a bit harder to simply luck one's way into the other Dharmas. In California, the Petals of Virtue are deeply embedded in Chinese-American culture, while the Chosen of God are among the Pakistani and Indian Muslim community, just to name two examples. Rather than a prohibition, this is simply an invitation to think deeply about your characters connections and what matters to them.<br /> <br /> 3) You're unusual, but you're not unique. The reach of Hungry Dead civilization has at times extended into Russia and into the Central Asian steppes, through the lands of eastern Persia and into the edges of Europe. Other characters are sure to note that you're different from the usual mold-- But by default, there is no assumption that you will be seen as a unicorn or an abomination, unless you specifically want to tell stories with those kinds of problems. </div> </div> </div>This is from the relentless age author's<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\"> RPG.net thread</a> where they talk about the development process of the game and lay out the many concepts intended for the final product. I don't know how much of it made into the final book but the thread is a good insight to they thought process of relentless age's author and a free preview to some material for relentless age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T02:48:18-07:00","id":1539007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1539005#post1539005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Kote The Relentless Age makes it clear that being the follower of the Dharmas isn't tired to ones race and it only takes a welling hungry dead to teach a respective student as this excerpt has shown:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is from the relentless age author's<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\"> RPG.net thread</a> where they talk about the development process of the game and lay out the many concepts intended for the final product. I don't know how much of it made into the final book but the thread is a good insight to they thought process of relentless age's author and a free preview to some material for relentless age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this and would play such a character.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm starting to imagine a &quot;Cain was actually a Kuei-jin who somehow got some special capacities and weaknesses compared to the others&quot; headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 07-22-2024, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T12:41:27-07:00","id":1541000,"title":"","content":"Good news! I bought Alma Maters for Hunter it\u2019s really good. Lots of solid lore with some hints about mages, wraiths and fae. Not convinced to change my mind about WoD5 yet, but this one book was really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T15:29:45-07:00","id":1541035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1541000#post1541000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news! I bought Alma Maters for Hunter it\u2019s really good. Lots of solid lore with some hints about mages, wraiths and fae. Not convinced to change my mind about WoD5 yet, but this one book was really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the like \ud83d\ude0a<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethys